Vikram and Betal: The Honest Woodcutter

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a poor woodcutter,” said Betal. “He earned his living by cutting wood in the forest.”

One day, while cutting wood near a river, his axe slipped from his hand and fell into the water.

The woodcutter became very sad.

Suddenly, a spirit appeared and said, “Why are you crying?”

The woodcutter explained what had happened.

The spirit went into the river and brought out a golden axe.

“Is this yours?” it asked.

The woodcutter replied, “No, that is not mine.”

Then the spirit brought a silver axe.

“Is this yours?” it asked again.

The woodcutter said, “No, my axe is made of iron.”

Finally, the spirit brought his iron axe.

The woodcutter was happy and said, “Yes, this is mine.”

The spirit was pleased with his honesty and gave him all three axes as a reward.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why was the woodcutter rewarded?”

Vikram replied, “Because he chose honesty over greed.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Honesty is always rewarded.
